[grammar(u,'二49','动词 + 好 / 完 / 到 / 见 / 懂 / 清楚','Check the resulting state rather than infer it from an action',
'做饭 names an activity; 做好饭 says the preparation reaches the intended ready state. 看完 says reading finished, 看懂 says it was understood, 看见 says something was perceived. 听清楚 is clearer perception, not necessarily comprehension. Negative result uses 没有: 没听清楚. Do not claim a safe temperature or successful outcome just because someone tried.',[('饭做好了，先等一下再端。','The meal is prepared; wait a little before serving.'),('我看完了，但还没看懂。','I finished reading but still have not understood.'),('没听清楚，请再说一次。','I did not hear clearly; please say it again.')],('我听了，所以一定听懂了。','我听了，但还没听懂。','Hearing an utterance does not guarantee comprehension.')),
grammar(u,'二50','动词 + 来 / 去；动词 + 上 / 下 / 进 / 出 / 回 / 过 / 起','Locate movement and its direction',
'端出来 is movement out toward the speaker or the scene’s reference point; 端出去 moves out away from it. 拿上 indicates movement upward, 拿下 downward, 拿进去 into somewhere. Mark the location before choosing 来/去. The directional complement is not proof that the object is cooked or that permission was granted.',[('我在门外，请端出来。','I am outside the door; please bring it out here.'),('你在屋里，把杯子拿出去。','You are inside; take the cup out away from there.'),('把书拿下来，再放回去。','Take the book down and then put it back.')],('我在门外，请端出去给我。这里以我为方向。','我在门外，请端出来给我。','Use toward the stated speaker as the reference direction.')),
grammar(u,'二57','同一主语 + 动词短语 + 动词短语','Recognize linked actions with one subject',
'我去商店买东西 uses the same subject for going and buying; buying is the purpose of the trip. 我拿杯子喝水 links taking a cup to drinking. Do not change the subject midway without stating it. A purpose is not a completed result: 去买 does not guarantee 买到.',[('我去商店买面。','I go to the shop to buy flour.'),('她拿杯子喝水。','She takes a cup to drink water.'),('他进厨房帮忙。','He enters the kitchen to help.')],('我去商店她买面。这要说我去买。','我去商店买面。','Keep the intended shared subject instead of inserting a different one.'))],
